WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:16.370
ROBERT WOODSON: I'm
Bob Woodson, president

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.170
of The Woodson Center.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:22.160
I'm here to talk about
race and economics.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.170
These two issues
in America did not

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:28.670
converge until the 1960s with
some pretty devastating effects

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:31.910
that I'll discuss in my remarks.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:34.820
But the character of any
nation or any individual

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:39.380
is determined by how we
treat the least of us.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.870
In America, the
moral barometer is

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:46.040
how we've treated Blacks in
America, and also low income

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.550
people.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:51.250
Just a little history of that.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:54.760
Prior to the 1960s,
the responsibility

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:58.730
for caring for those
who are in need

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:03.100
and various ethnic
groups and racial groups

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.980
was the responsibility
of private institutions

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:08.550
within those groups.

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:11.520
Immigrants coming
from the backwaters

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.300
of Eastern and Southern
Europe, they came here.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:18.990
The first requirement was
to become acculturated,

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:23.140
and also they must
be assimilated.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:25.720
And assimilation meant they
had to learn the language

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:27.970
and learn the customs
and acculturation.

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:32.720
They had to learn the customs
of the country as well.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:36.250
Well, the large cities
proved to be a melting pot

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:38.690
and a place of
assimilation took place.

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:41.990
And the civic institutions
within these communities,

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:47.240
these cities, did a great job
of producing Americans out

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.120
of these immigrants.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.890
In the Black community,
the same process

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:57.230
emerged that even under
segregation and discrimination,

00:01:57.230 --> 00:02:01.580
there was a rich array of
civic institutions, churches,

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:05.840
Masonic organizations that
rose up within the groups

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:09.070
to provide for those in need.

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:11.350
One of the largest
was in Philadelphia

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:16.570
during Free Blacks in
1789, Mother Bethel Church.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:20.680
But even among free Blacks
who sought assistance

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:24.460
from their church, there were
high moral standards for people

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:25.990
who qualified for aid.

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:30.610
You couldn't get assistance if
your poverty or your situation

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:35.310
was caused by your own
slothfulness or immorality.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:39.820
So high standards were always
required for those receiving

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:41.080
aid.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:44.320
And this continued
up until the 1930s

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:48.510
with the crash of
the stock market.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:50.530
Pressure mounted on
these institutions,

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:56.170
so they could not continue
to provide for their people.

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:59.340
And so government intervened for
the first time in the economy

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:02.850
on behalf of low income people
and people who were struggling,

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:07.510
but intervention was largely
government to individuals.

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:11.430
And so as a result, these
civic institutions pretty much

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:15.520
stayed intact until the 1960s.

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:17.840
This all changed.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:23.330
For the Black community up until
1965, 85% of all households

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:26.610
had a man and a woman
raising children.

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:30.360
But a lot of that changed in
the '60s after the Voting Rights

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:37.150
Act passed and we had
the Watts Riots occurred.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:40.270
And Lyndon Johnson announced
his war on poverty.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:47.770
As a result of these events,
liberal social scientists

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:53.930
at Columbia University School of
Social Work, Cloward and Piven,

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:56.000
came up with a
social construct that

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.720
says that the Black community--

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:03.170
if we want to really
emphasize the contradictions

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:05.540
of capitalism, that
one of the ways

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:13.400
that we can do that is to
insist that welfare to Blacks

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:17.250
be given as reparations.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:21.540
And at the time
public aid to Blacks

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:24.720
was really stigmatized
in the Black community.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:28.380
To overcome that stigmatization
the social scientists

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:31.770
at the time began to
promote the notion

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:34.140
that the nuclear
family was eurocentric

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:36.090
and therefore racist.

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:39.120
They concluded that if we
can separate work from income

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:41.750
and replace it with
welfare, it would make

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:44.640
fathers redundant in homes.

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:48.030
Well, this social construct was
supported by the Black Power

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:52.860
movement that saw the nuclear
family, too, as eurocentric.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:57.210
Also, welfare policies
were destigmatized.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:00.350
It was considered reparations.

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:03.410
But just having a social
policy alone was not enough.

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:06.290
The federal government,
through the opportunity offices

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:09.500
and the poverty
programs, actually opened

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:13.130
government offices and
actively recruited Blacks

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:16.290
into the welfare system.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:19.890
Privacy laws, suits were filed
so that women who were pregnant

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:24.510
out of wedlock no longer
had to declare paternity

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:28.240
as a condition of
them getting welfare.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:30.960
And so it's the
combination of these events

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:33.900
that you saw the
explosion of welfare.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:38.280
People, millions began to
flow into the welfare system.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:40.230
The liberal social
scientists concluded

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:44.070
that if we could only
bankrupt our cities,

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:45.510
then the federal
government would

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:51.480
be compelled to change how
we address poverty by having

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:53.020
income redistribution.

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:56.190
So it was really socialist
aims at the time.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:58.860
And the Black
community was the agent

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:02.760
through which they would
promote this dramatic change.

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:05.700
And as a consequence,
millions of Blacks

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:09.000
flowed into the welfare
system at a time in New York

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:14.330
when the unemployment rate
for Black men was under 4%.

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:18.530
And so what was predicted
actually came true.

00:06:18.530 --> 00:06:21.800
There was an explosion
of out of wedlock births,

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:26.540
and so that number
of Black Americans,

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:30.320
Black family
formation rates went

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:35.540
from 85% out of
wedlock births to 70%,

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.930
and all the accompanying
social pathology followed--

00:06:38.930 --> 00:06:45.260
dropout rates, violence,
disintegration of families.

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:49.550
All of these pathologies
occurred at one time

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:50.570
in the Black community.

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:53.660
And in '73, New York
City did, in fact,

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:57.360
go bankrupt because of
the explosion of welfare.

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:01.550
And this decline
was used by the left

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:04.700
to justify racial antagonism.

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:09.770
They said now that these
changes that are occurring

00:07:09.770 --> 00:07:13.470
were a direct result of
racial discrimination.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:22.050
1619 came along
in August of 2019.

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:25.440
This was really the fulfillment
of the policies that

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:31.350
started in the '60s, that the
1619 Project from The New York

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:35.760
Times began to look at
the problems facing Black

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:38.160
America today, the
out of wedlock births,

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:41.040
the explosion of
Black on Black crime.

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:46.590
More Blacks were killed in
one year by other Blacks

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:51.990
than were killed in 40 years
lynchings in the South.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:56.010
In other words, Black
American neighborhoods

00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:59.970
had a 9/11 every six months.

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:07.940
And so the architects of
1619 associated those changes

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:11.270
with a legacy of slavery
and discrimination.

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:15.440
And they said because the
real birthday of America

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:22.160
is 1619, that that was the
date that in Jamestown, 20

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:27.470
African slaves arrived, and so
America should be defined not

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:33.770
from 1776, but 1619, that the
arrival of slave in America

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:38.690
is incurably racist, and all
white people are villains

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:40.490
and therefore to be punished.

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:46.790
And all Blacks are
victims to be compensated.

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:49.880
And that became the
dominant narrative

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:53.450
that replaced the civil rights
proposition that we should

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:55.500
be judged by the
content of our character

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:57.320
and not the color of our skin.

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:02.450
But that has now been replaced
with intersectionality,

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:06.530
and race grievance is
the primary definition

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:11.380
of what social activists
are engaged in today.

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:14.070
And so what we at
the Woodson Center

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:19.920
are doing with our 1776
campaign, what we're

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:25.890
doing with the 1776 campaign is
we're challenging this notion

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:30.570
that America should be defined
by its birth defect of slavery,

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:34.020
but America should be
defined by its promise

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:36.490
of equal opportunity.

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:39.280
And what we are doing
by assembling scholars

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:43.120
and activists is not
enough to challenge

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:47.410
the intellectual
framework of 1619

00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:52.690
because we believe that
experience will always

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:54.430
triumph over an argument.

00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:56.200
Therefore, what
we have recruited

00:09:56.200 --> 00:10:01.570
are not only Black scholars
that are presenting essays

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:06.320
to repudiate the
statements in 1619.

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:09.200
But also, we bring
along activists

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:13.130
whose lives are the embodiment
of the founding principles

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:16.010
of personal responsibility.

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:20.930
And so to challenge this
notion, we have given evidence.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:28.460
For instance, in 1920 to
1940, the education gap

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:30.410
in the South between
Blacks and whites

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:36.260
was eighth grade for whites,
it was fifth grade for Blacks.

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:41.390
But because Julius Rosenwald,
the Jewish CEO of Sears,

00:10:41.390 --> 00:10:44.780
partnered with
Booker T. Washington,

00:10:44.780 --> 00:10:49.700
and Rosenwald put up $4
million, and the Black community

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:51.500
raised $4.8 million.

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:54.920
And together this partnership,
the Black community

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:59.630
built 5,000 Rosenwald
schools in the deep South

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:04.400
to provide education to
untutored and uneducated

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:05.570
Blacks.

00:11:05.570 --> 00:11:13.460
And as a consequence of this
effort, between 1920 and 1940,

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:17.180
just 20 years, the
education gap in the South

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:21.860
closed from three
years to six months.

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:26.510
When Blacks were denied
access to hotels,

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:28.470
they built their own hotels.

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:32.690
In every major city,
there was a major hotel.

00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:36.080
In Chicago, Illinois,
for instance,

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:41.560
in 1929, in the
Bronzeville section,

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:46.510
Blacks owned 731 businesses.

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:50.590
We had $100 million
in real estate assets.

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:56.380
So all over America, in the
presence of discrimination,

00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:59.620
Black Americans,
using the instruments

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:03.670
of the free enterprise system,
pooled their money together

00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:05.860
in their churches'
burial societies

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:10.450
and capitalized their own
businesses and thrived.

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:14.050
They had Black Wall
Streets all over America.

00:12:14.050 --> 00:12:17.510
Throughout the history
of this country,

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:23.890
Black Americans have fought
in every war in defense

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:27.690
of the founding principles.

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:32.370
And what we should
celebrate is their success

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:34.445
within the context
of the system.

00:12:34.445 --> 00:12:36.570
If we're going to talk
about the legacy of slavery,

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:38.640
we should also talk
about the legacy

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:42.670
of resistance and
resilience, that Blacks

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:44.860
resisted by being resilient.

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:50.710
For instance, in 1943, there
were no Black Naval officers,

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:54.340
so Eleanor Roosevelt, the
wife of President Roosevelt,

00:12:54.340 --> 00:13:00.310
insisted that the Navy
train Black Naval officers.

00:13:00.310 --> 00:13:05.650
The Navy selected 16
college-educated Black cadets

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:07.450
for training.

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:11.470
But they decided to
give these Black cadets

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:17.470
in eight weeks what they would
give white cadets in 16 weeks.

00:13:17.470 --> 00:13:23.150
And once the Black cadets found
out what the Navy was about,

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:25.300
they put blankets up
over their windows

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:27.490
and stayed up all
night and studied.

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:29.410
And when they were
tested, they all

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:33.330
scored in the 90th percentile.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:36.910
Well, the Navy, believing
that they had cheated,

00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:39.650
tested them individually.

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:45.160
The second time they scored
in the 93rd percentile.

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:50.500
And after a few months
of hesitation, 13 of them

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:53.410
were made officers
for the first time.

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:58.820
To this day, the
scores of these cadets

00:13:58.820 --> 00:14:02.310
set a record at the
Academy because they

00:14:02.310 --> 00:14:07.710
have the highest score in the
history of the Naval Training

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:08.850
Academy.

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:11.160
Another example from history
that we're presenting

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:13.110
is a man named
Robert Smalls, who

00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:20.610
was born in 1839 in
[INAUDIBLE] North Carolina.

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:24.390
He was a slave
working on a ship.

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:34.320
And one night, when his
masters he left the ship,

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:36.480
he commandeered the ship.

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:39.540
And along with his
five other crewmen,

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:44.160
they sneaked out of the port,
picked up their families,

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:48.060
and put their master's hat
on, and waved and went past

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:51.840
five different garrison and
turned the supply ship over

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:54.690
to the Union Navy.

00:14:54.690 --> 00:14:57.900
Robert Smalls was celebrated
throughout the country,

00:14:57.900 --> 00:15:01.410
and as a consequence
of his heroic actions,

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:06.500
Lincoln admitted Blacks in
to fight for the Union Army.

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:11.870
After the war, Robert Smalls
became a successful businessman

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:16.670
and got elected to the
Congress during Reconstruction.

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:19.460
And he went back and
purchased the plantation

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:22.250
on which he was a slave.

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:24.800
And because the family
of the slave master

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:29.780
had become destitute, in
an act of radical grace,

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:34.100
he took in the wife and
children of the slave master

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:38.150
and even allowed her to
remain in the master bedroom,

00:15:38.150 --> 00:15:41.660
as she had become
delusional and didn't

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:45.870
realize that the war was over.

00:15:45.870 --> 00:15:50.300
And I think that's a marvelous
story of the resilience

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:56.120
of Black Americans to thrive
and achieve against the odds,

00:15:56.120 --> 00:16:00.275
to be born a slave, and through
the free enterprise system,

00:16:00.275 --> 00:16:03.140
earn enough money to
come back and actually

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:06.410
purchase the plantation
of which he was a slave

00:16:06.410 --> 00:16:08.720
and exhibited the
kind of radical grace

00:16:08.720 --> 00:16:11.330
that enabled him
to take in and care

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:15.140
for the family of
the slave master.

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:18.980
And so we are taking
these experiences that

00:16:18.980 --> 00:16:23.570
are ignored and
overlooked by 1619

00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:28.820
and presenting these as evidence
that America should not ever

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:34.280
be defined by its birth
defect of slavery,

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:39.130
but it should be defined by
the promise that it holds.

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:43.130
And that's why people of
color from all over the world

00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:46.190
are risking their
lives to get here.

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:49.940
And so it is important
because the message that

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:58.410
is coming from liberal radical
leftists and the Black Lives

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:01.680
Matter movement
is really sending

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:06.030
a very dangerous message to
not only Blacks, but whites.

00:17:06.030 --> 00:17:09.780
And the message that
is being sent to Blacks

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:14.819
is that they are defined by
slavery and discrimination.

00:17:14.819 --> 00:17:18.190
And therefore, if white
America doesn't change,

00:17:18.190 --> 00:17:21.990
it is difficult, impossible
for Blacks to change.

00:17:21.990 --> 00:17:26.730
That's making an assumption
that Blacks have no agency

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:30.270
and therefore are
totally dependent.

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:33.210
But our society
is at a crossroads

00:17:33.210 --> 00:17:38.860
right now where race is
dominating everything.

00:17:38.860 --> 00:17:46.690
Contracts between law firms now
require that companies sign on

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:50.540
to the race grievance training.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:54.710
School systems are
being taught history

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:58.430
that America is
defined by slavery.

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:00.340
And so our culture
is being polluted

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:05.900
by this notion that America
is defined by slavery

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:08.540
and that it is an
exploitative nation

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:13.220
and capitalism is
to be disavowed.

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:16.760
The Black Lives Matter
movement promotes itself

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:21.440
as seeking social
justice in wake

00:18:21.440 --> 00:18:27.450
of George Floyd being murdered
or killed by the police.

00:18:27.450 --> 00:18:30.440
But what they have done
is hijack the civil rights

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:35.180
movement and migrated it
from justice for Blacks

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:38.510
to burning Bibles in
Portland, to attempting

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:41.660
to desecrate World
War II memorials,

00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:45.350
taking down statues not
of Southern generals,

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:50.560
but of luminaries like
Frederick Douglass.

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:53.950
And so there really
is a crisis in America

00:18:53.950 --> 00:19:01.110
where the radical left is using
race and America's birth defect

00:19:01.110 --> 00:19:06.290
as a bludgeon to tear
apart this nation.

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:09.580
And so what we
believe should happen

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:15.670
as a defense of this nation is
that the majority of low income

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:21.130
Blacks who are suffering
the most in this turmoil

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:24.580
that we're in, they are
also the greatest allies

00:19:24.580 --> 00:19:27.460
in the restoration
of this nation.

00:19:27.460 --> 00:19:33.250
I think there is a myth that
the so-called spokespersons

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:37.390
for Black Americans speaks for
the everyday Black American.

00:19:37.390 --> 00:19:39.220
It's just not true.

00:19:39.220 --> 00:19:42.930
Many of those who
command the microphones

00:19:42.930 --> 00:19:47.760
and are on the talk shows
supposed to be representatives

00:19:47.760 --> 00:19:53.310
of the poor, many of these
leaders are against the police.

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:58.350
80% of Black Americans support
more police in communities.

00:19:58.350 --> 00:20:00.360
There's always
been a bifurcation

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:03.690
between the interests of
so-called spokesperson

00:20:03.690 --> 00:20:05.550
and low income people.

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:08.520
For instance, on the issue
of vouchers and choice

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:12.090
in education, only 8% of
the so-called civil rights

00:20:12.090 --> 00:20:14.760
leadership supports vouchers.

00:20:14.760 --> 00:20:20.880
65% to 70% of low income
Blacks support vouchers.

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:22.030
And this is true.

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:28.230
For instance, in Florida
the 2018 election

00:20:28.230 --> 00:20:30.420
gubernatorial election
where deSantis

00:20:30.420 --> 00:20:37.980
ran against Gillum, the liberal
Black former mayor of Tampa,

00:20:37.980 --> 00:20:41.550
the margin of victory
was 32,000 votes.

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:44.820
And that's because
100,000 low income Blacks

00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:48.420
voted for the Republican
deSantis because

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:50.700
of his position on
choice and vouchers

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:55.380
in education, even though
Gillum brought into the campaign

00:20:55.380 --> 00:21:02.690
for him ex-President
Obama and Oprah Winfrey.

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:04.790
Even with Oprah
Winfrey and Obama

00:21:04.790 --> 00:21:07.010
coming to campaign for
the Black candidate,

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:11.090
100,000 low income Blacks
voted the other way

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:15.290
because they put the interests
of their children's education

00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:18.010
ahead of race.

00:21:18.010 --> 00:21:19.920
And I think that is
an opening, and you're

00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:25.710
going to see the same divide
as you take specific issues

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:26.880
into communities.

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:30.180
After all, many of
those who are advocating

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:32.190
the defunding of
the police do not

00:21:32.190 --> 00:21:36.390
live in neighborhoods that
have high crime rates.

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:39.600
Many of them live in
gated communities,

00:21:39.600 --> 00:21:42.720
and therefore they don't have
to suffer the consequences

00:21:42.720 --> 00:21:43.877
of their advocacy.

00:21:43.877 --> 00:21:45.210
What is it they're trying to do?

00:21:45.210 --> 00:21:47.760
Because they have no solutions.

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:51.840
All they're talking about
is what they are against,

00:21:51.840 --> 00:21:58.010
what they want to abolish,
what they want to deconstruct.

00:21:58.010 --> 00:22:01.440
They offer no remedies.

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:04.050
They are saying that the
problem of Black America

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:06.690
is institutional racism.

00:22:06.690 --> 00:22:10.200
My challenge to them
is what does that mean?

00:22:10.200 --> 00:22:13.440
Give me an example of
institutional racism.

00:22:13.440 --> 00:22:16.800
And then I want to know what
remedy would they apply?

00:22:16.800 --> 00:22:18.630
And then how would
that remedy stop,

00:22:18.630 --> 00:22:20.940
for instance, the
hemorrhage of Black

00:22:20.940 --> 00:22:24.270
on Black death in
the inner city?

00:22:24.270 --> 00:22:27.540
How would it reduce
drug addictions

00:22:27.540 --> 00:22:33.610
among vulnerable populations
living in our inner cities?

00:22:33.610 --> 00:22:39.670
So one of the ways that
America can be restored

00:22:39.670 --> 00:22:44.590
is if we mobilize within
low income neighborhoods

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:50.380
those people that stand to
lose the most because now what

00:22:50.380 --> 00:22:54.690
the left is saying
to Black America,

00:22:54.690 --> 00:22:59.240
that you are exempt from
any personal responsibility

00:22:59.240 --> 00:23:02.330
for control of your
life, that you can never

00:23:02.330 --> 00:23:06.920
be agents of your own uplift,
that the bourgeois values

00:23:06.920 --> 00:23:11.720
of hard work, sacrifice, delayed
gratification are somehow

00:23:11.720 --> 00:23:17.000
associated with colonialism
or white suppression.

00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:21.920
And therefore, to be
legitimately Black,

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:25.100
you must abandon
the bourgeois values

00:23:25.100 --> 00:23:28.070
that enabled Frederick
Douglass and many

00:23:28.070 --> 00:23:32.780
of those who came before us
in the past who successfully

00:23:32.780 --> 00:23:36.830
fought against racial
discrimination and oppression

00:23:36.830 --> 00:23:41.150
by building their
own schools, building

00:23:41.150 --> 00:23:47.190
their own mental hospitals,
hotels, educational systems.

00:23:47.190 --> 00:23:49.610
So the true liberators
of this country

00:23:49.610 --> 00:23:53.180
will be those in whose name
Black Lives Matter have

00:23:53.180 --> 00:23:56.000
defamed by their actions.

00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:58.910
The Golden 13 example,
and the example

00:23:58.910 --> 00:24:02.210
of the life of Robert
Small, are just

00:24:02.210 --> 00:24:07.130
a few examples of what I
call radical grace in action,

00:24:07.130 --> 00:24:12.960
and they really exemplify
the best that is America.

00:24:12.960 --> 00:24:16.800
We must come together
and deracialize

00:24:16.800 --> 00:24:22.010
race and desegregate
poverty, and try

00:24:22.010 --> 00:24:29.510
to assist all Americans to
be the best that we can be.

00:24:29.510 --> 00:24:31.360
Thank you.

